Snapshot 2026-09-26 (i265): RDOQ `optimize_b` per-call cost vs C
(Phase 5 item 7 — brief `optimize-b`).

Cell A: `perf_encode gradient 1024 1024 40 10 <prefix> 0` vs
`tools/perf_c_encode/perf_c_encode 1024 1024 40 10 <prefix>.yuv c.obu 0`
(mainline-4.2.0 oracle library). Cell B: 256x256 p6, same form.

Change (all byte-identical; `quant.rs` + `entropy/coeff_c.rs` only):

- `dqv`: the QM inverse-weight multiply ran unconditionally
  (`(dqv * 32 + 16) >> 5`, an identity). Now matches C `get_dqv`
  (full_loop.c:741): a single `dequant[!!ci]` read when `iwt` is None —
  the whole measured cell runs no-QM.
- `get_br_ctx`/`get_br_ctx_eob` hoisted out of `coeff_cost_general` /
  `coeff_cost_eob`: the trellis calls each twice per coefficient (level
  and level-1 candidates) against a `levels` map that is not written
  between them, so one computation serves both. C recomputes per call.
- Loop-invariant bounds stated once per `optimize_b` call
  (`tx_size < 19`, `bwl <= 5`, `n <= 1024`, `dc_sign_ctx < 3`) and once
  per coefficient (`ci < n`, buffers sliced to `n`, `scan` sliced to the
  entry eob) plus `bwl <= 5` inside `nz_mag_tc`/`br_ctx_tc` and the
  `eob_pos_token` group bound — LLVM then folds the per-tap and
  per-table bounds checks into those asserts. Each assert restates an
  invariant whose violation already panicked on an index today.
- `update_coeff_eob` tests the tracked final `qc` instead of reloading
  `qcoeff[ci]`.

callgrind Ir (`tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh`; valgrind 3.22):

